\section{Spacetime Foliation and Tensor Definitions}

Let $(M, g_{\mu\nu})$ be a smooth, globally hyperbolic spacetime manifold
admitting a foliation into spacelike hypersurfaces $\Sigma_t$.
The line element is decomposed via the ADM formalism:
\[
ds^2 = -\alpha^2 dt^2 + \gamma_{ij}
\left(dx^i + \beta^i dt\right)
\left(dx^j + \beta^j dt\right),
\]
where $\alpha$ is the lapse function, $\beta^i$ is the shift vector,
and $\gamma_{ij}$ is the induced 3-metric on $\Sigma_t$.

The extrinsic curvature tensor is defined by
\[
K_{ij} = -\frac{1}{2\alpha}
\left(\partial_t \gamma_{ij}
- \mathcal{D}_i \beta_j
- \mathcal{D}_j \beta_i\right),
\]
with $\mathcal{D}_i$ the covariant derivative compatible with $\gamma_{ij}$.

